CONTRIS! (running in a CON:-Window :-) is an easy-to-use 8-Color
ANSI-Game with some nice

Features:
~~~~~~~~~
- running in CLI or BBS (simple to install on DLG Pro-Systems)
- quite fast (maybe we can speed it up a bit..)
- different sets of High-Score-tables in dayly, weekly, monthly
  manner, High-Score-table for each user, All-Time-Heros..
- multiuser-friendly (in earlier versions, HiScore tables got messed
  up when playing in more tasks at the same time :-)
- standard ANSI-sequences should work with any
  IBM-8-Color-ANSI-Terminal. (tested with JRCOMM 8-color-IBM, NComm,
  Platinum Online!, Telemate..)
- the speed now results in the number of lines you have cleared,
  after 50 lines it get's NOT faster. (highscore when beta-testing
  with 2400 baud: more than 2000 points, highscore on local session
  more than 3000 points (both: Kai Bolay ;-) )

Bugs:
~~~~~
- CONTRIS! is sending multiple Screen-Clears to make sure that ANY
  Terminal will understand one of them... (^L Esc-[0c...)
  JRComm seems to get problems with this when not set up properly..
  this wil cause JRComm to crash... make sure you have IBM-8-Colors
  and no special fonts or keymaps activated...
  Online! and NComm make no probs at all...

(To Jack Radigan: we don't think that it's OK to be able to KILL JRComm
 just by sending some weird :-) ANSI-Sequences and that this is a bug
 in JRComm 1.01..., not a bug in CONTRIS! !!! Fix it, pleeaaaze...)

- when not set up properly with DLG Pro (handler flags...), your
  system will be completely locked up !!! Be careful when
  installing !!!

Future Plans:
~~~~~~~~~~~~~
- remove all reported bugs :-)
- multi-player-version with message-ports and gags like adding lines
  to other players... (ready when DLG Pro V1.0 is out :-)
- FidoNet-World-Top-Ten with automatic Netmail-Routing of the
  Top-Ten-lists (could be done once in a month by some user CONTRIS!
  on any DLG-System attached to the DLG_PR or DLG_INFO Echos....)
  This is a FAR plan we might add somedays, but it should be
  possible (maybe when DLG Pro V 2.0 is out :-)
- A real coin-up-like version with different levels and
  level-editor...
- anything you tell us and that is possible...


Attention:
~~~~~~~~~~
From v 2.5 (this release) on Contris! will be released in a DLG-hardcoded
version, which requires the following assignments:

USER:   --> the path where the user-directories are
Doors:  --> this is where the highscores will be saved (I think most
            systems will have this already, so no harm done :-)
           (if you register, you may specify any other path :-)

Contris! v2.5 requires DLG:DF to display the Helpfile
"Doors:Contris.help", which you can edit as you like.
We decided so, because you can use any of DLG's switches and you can
write your helpfile in your mother-language. (A German and English
one are included in this distribution-archive)

Since we've seen so much people using Contris! and so many (ONE !!)
people register, we decided to release v2.5 as a crippled version:

Each user can only play ONCE each day. When registering, this limit
will be removed (or, if you like, we can set it to any other value :-)

Thanks to Leon D. Shaner for registering, YOU will be the first one
to get a full working copy :-)


Installation on DLG Pro Systems:
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

Make a new menu-entry:

command-type is (1) executable program:

should be like:

Doors:CONTRIS/CONTRIS "%UNAME"
                        ^
                        +--------------- players underscored name

(I don't know right now, but could be that it works with %NAME, too)

The handler-flags are as follows:

  Reload menu                    YES
  Enable Ctrl-C break            NO
  Enable Ctrl-D break            NO
  Enable <CR><LF>                YES
  Enable echo                    NO
  Enable process killing         YES
  Enable kill pending            YES
  Enable PassThru mode           NO
  Enable pausing                 YES
  Enable RAW mode                YES
  Enable timeouts                YES
  Enable verbose pause           NO
  Enable line freezing           NO


We know that THESE flags WORK, if you try to change some of them,
your system could lock up when playing on multiple lines...
so don't change anything !!


